<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBData
      Source: StGB consolidated, data and privacy offences (provenance StGB 202a, 202b, 202c, 202d; German governs)
      Rebuilt to the current encoding contract, superseding the earlier data-offences carrier; 263a, 303a and 303b
      remain in their own carrier unchanged. The 202a scope authors [ProtectedData] (the Section 202a(2) definition),
      consumed by name by the 202b, 202c and 202d scopes. The 202c scope keeps the Section 149(2),(3) repentance
      reference live per the markup (input resolution; contrast the struck Section 129(7)); the 202d scope carries the
      live lawful-duties exemption [LawfulDutyExemption] and retains the enrichment-or-harm intent per the retention
      criterion. Sanctions, the 202b and 107b-pattern subsidiarity clauses and the 202d(2) penalty cap struck.
      Runtime caveat: consolidated file, not a proven executable, until the loader's scope-local resolution is tested.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Data and Privacy Offences (§202a to §202d)</Subject><Verb>protect</Verb><Article>StGB 202a, 202b, 202c, 202d</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBData</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

